---
/*
  ═══ Operating System — sept principes (BRIEF §7) ═══

  MEME TRAITEMENT QUE PHILOSOPHY, et pour la meme raison : ce n'est pas une
  etude de cas. Pas de chiffres cles, pas de trois temps - sept principes, qui
  se tiennent ensemble plutot que de se raconter l'un apres l'autre.

  LA COMPOSITION PORTE TOUT, Y COMPRIS LE TEXTE. Elle etait un sommaire : sept
  cases commandaient sept <section> posees dessous. Les sections sont parties,
  le texte est remonte DANS les cases, et la page ne sort plus de sa grille -
  le meme geste que Philosophy.

  LES SEPT SE REPLIENT, ET C'EST LA REGLE QUI LE DIT. Si la description tient
  dans la case elle se lit sous le titre, sinon la case se replie sur son titre
  et s'ouvre au clic. Ici aucune ne tient : les sept descriptions font 550,
  550, 599, 614, 714, 939 et 1 154 signes, quand les trois que Philosophy
  montre d'emblee font 228, 310 et 317. La plus courte d'Operating System est
  encore 70 % plus longue que la plus longue de Philosophy - une case qui la
  porterait ne serait plus une case, ce serait une colonne de texte. Cette
  page-ci est la plus dense des deux ; le pli y est la regle, pas l'exception.

  CE QUI CHANGE QUAND MEME AU REPOS, et c'est l'essentiel : les aplats sont
  poses des le trace au lieu d'etre gagnes au clic. La grille se lit comme un
  Mondrian tout de suite - rouge, blanc, jaune, bleu - au lieu de sept cartes
  blanches a devoiler.

  LA CHARNIERE A DISPARU, et son propos est remonte dans l'intro du hero. Elle
  etait un bandeau noir entre la composition et les sections, avec le disque
  des mains : « Same principle, top to bottom: everyone gets to own their
  part. » Les sections parties, elle n'avait plus rien a charnieres - et Lea a
  reecrit l'intro pour qu'elle porte elle-meme cette phrase, en chute de son
  troisieme paragraphe. Son visuel est parti avec elle : collective-ownership-
  visual.svg etait le seul fichier de src/assets/operating-system, qui ne
  porte donc plus rien que git suive.

  LA CLOTURE ENTRE DANS LA GRILLE. Elle prend la place que la citation
  « Cultivating practice… » occupe sur la landing : une case blanche, sa phrase
  en gros, son bouton cale en bas.

  TOUT LE TEXTE DES SEPT PRINCIPES EST CONSERVE, y compris le bandeau de
  sobriete - trois tuiles, le dispositif du gabarit pour un terme et sa
  definition. Elles passent a UNE colonne : dans une case de 515px, trois
  colonnes en feraient 135 chacune. Seuls les <em> de couleur des phrases
  d'attaque tombent sur les cases de couleur, ou un mot rouge sur un aplat
  rouge ne se verrait pas.

  LES SEPT CASES SONT ECRITES, PAS DERIVEES D'UN TABLEAU. Elles l'etaient, et
  c'etait possible tant que les cases ne contenaient rien. Maintenant que
  chacune porte sa description - avec ses <p>, ses <strong>, sa citation et ses
  tuiles - ce contenu est du markup : il ne rentre pas dans une chaine. On perd
  la renumerotation automatique ; c'est sept valeurs sur une page qui ne bouge
  plus souvent.

  L'ORDRE DU DOM EST 01 → 07 puis la cloture : c'est l'ordre de lecture.
  `grid-area` fait le placement au-dessus de 861px, le flux fait l'empilement
  en dessous.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/etude.css';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Conviction from '../components/Conviction.astro';
import Tuiles from '../components/Tuiles.astro';
import type { Tuile } from '../components/Tuiles.astro';
import Bouton from '../components/Bouton.astro';

/*
  Les trois formes de la sobriete. Le decoupage terme / chute n'est pas force :
  le document source ecrivait deja ces trois points en deux temps. Elles
  sortent du corps du principe 03 et deviennent trois tuiles, le dispositif du
  gabarit pour un terme et sa definition.
*/
const sobriete: Tuile[] = [
  { eyebrow: 'Light', couleur: 'rouge', titre: 'By default.',
    texte: 'Smallest possible package weight, and modular imports - teams pulled only the components they needed, never the whole library, so production sites stayed lean. <strong>A lighter system reaches more people, on more devices, with less energy.</strong>' },
  { eyebrow: 'Quiet', couleur: 'bleu', titre: 'By design.',
    texte: 'The system stayed deliberately sober, so brands could express themselves without fighting it. <strong>Restraint as a feature, not a limitation.</strong>' },
  { eyebrow: 'Fewer components', couleur: 'noir', titre: 'More coverage.',
    texte: 'Simple, flexible component architectures - the smallest set that meets the widest need, instead of a library that sprawls. Same for patterns: I ran a rationalization pass to keep them coherent across every product and positioned as standards.' },
];
---
<Base
  title="Operating System - Léa Giezek"
  description="How my team ships: discovery as a gate, one source of truth, accessibility as the floor, ethics before AI, and distributed ownership holding it together."
  noindex
>

  <Hero
    courant="operating-system"
    eyebrow="Operating System · How my team ships"
    filigrane="Ownership"
  >
    Seven principles designed to be handed over, each with a practice behind it.
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      <p><b>I didn't want a team that executes. I wanted a team of owners.</b>
      Recognized, proactive - experts with a name, a face, not just a pair of
      hands.</p>
      <p>Everything below is how I built that, and it runs on one conviction:
      the technical system and the human system obey the same rule. Design
      tokens make products autonomous, distributed ownership makes people
      autonomous.</p>
      <p><b>One variable in common: trust. One prerequisite: top to frontline,
      everyone gets to own their part.</b></p>
    </Fragment>
  </Hero>

  <div class="etude">

    {/*
      ─── La composition des sept principes ───
      Six colonnes, six rangees, deux colonnes fines (la 3 et la 6) qui ne
      portent que du decor : ce sont elles qui empechent les cases de se lire
      comme un tableau. Les rangees sont des planchers et non des hauteurs -
      une case qui s'ouvre fait grandir sa rangee au lieu d'etre rognee.
    */}
    <div class="compo compo--principes" id="composition" data-grille>

      <Conviction
        id="pr-discovery" rang="01" intitule="Discovery" couleur="rouge"
        titre="Nothing ships without discovery."
        aire="1 / 1 / 3 / 3" pliante large
      >
        <p>No component, no line of the roadmap ever shipped on a hunch. Every one started with the same work: what does the product ecosystem actually need, and what already exists that we can build on? <strong>Need first, existing second, decision third.</strong></p>
        <p>It's how we knew what to build versus what to buy - and it's the discipline I put in place after learning, the hard way, what it costs to build for the brand instead of the people who adopt it. <strong>Discovery isn't a phase. It's the gate.</strong> And it doesn't stop at launch: we kept interviewing, testing our own ways of working, and reprioritizing against what we heard.</p>
      </Conviction>

      {/* Les deux colonnes fines. Posees apres la premiere case pour que
          l'ordre du DOM reste celui de la lecture. */}
      <div class="compo__decor" aria-hidden="true" style="grid-area:1 / 3 / 2 / 4"><span class="compo__plat compo__plat--noir"></span></div>
      <div class="compo__decor" aria-hidden="true" style="grid-area:2 / 3 / 3 / 4"></div>

      <Conviction
        id="pr-truth" rang="02" intitule="Source of truth" couleur="clair"
        titre="One source of truth - trusted by humans, verified by machines."
        aire="1 / 4 / 2 / 7" pliante
      >
        <p>One language, not four. <strong>Multi-surface design tokens</strong> carry brand and behavior across web, native and content; <strong>Figma variables</strong> hold the component architecture on the design side; <strong>Storybook</strong> is the engineering source of truth on the code side.</p>
        <p>And trust doesn't mean unchecked: every pull request runs <strong>automated conformity checks before a double human validation</strong>, and <strong>Chromatic</strong> catches visual regressions before they ship. I ran the team on live signal too - <strong>DORA metrics every sprint</strong>, satisfaction surveys, ritual feedback - read as decisions, not dashboards for show. Automate the repeatable, measure what matters, keep the human judgment where it counts. <strong>That's governance you can't skip and don't have to police.</strong></p>
      </Conviction>

      <Conviction
        id="pr-inclusion" rang="03" intitule="Inclusion" couleur="jaune"
        titre="Accessibility is the floor. Responsibility is the reach."
        aire="2 / 4 / 4 / 6" pliante
      >
        <p><strong>WCAG AA</strong> wasn't our bar - I positioned it as the Sanofi digital standard, the minimum for every product, not just the library. We audited the full library to <strong>100% compliance before our first major</strong>, then held it there through continuous review - axe embedded, Storybook's native checks, manual review on top - so no product team paid the accessibility cost downstream.</p>
        <p>But inclusion doesn't stop at who can <em>use</em> the product. A system touching 45+ products has a footprint - societal and environmental - and it isn't small. So responsibility was designed in, not bolted on, and it looked like <strong>sobriety</strong> at every level.</p>
        <p class="qt">Accessibility protects the user. Responsibility protects everything around them. <strong>Same driver - inclusion - different reach.</strong></p>
        <p class="eb">Sobriety, at every level</p>
        <Tuiles tuiles={sobriete} colonnes={1} label="The three forms of sobriety" hauteur={280} />
      </Conviction>

      <div class="compo__decor" aria-hidden="true" style="grid-area:2 / 6 / 3 / 7"><span class="compo__plat compo__plat--gris"></span></div>
      <div class="compo__decor" aria-hidden="true" style="grid-area:3 / 6 / 4 / 7"><span class="compo__plat compo__plat--rouge"></span></div>

      <Conviction
        id="pr-ethics" rang="04" intitule="Ethics" couleur="bleu"
        titre="AI should earn trust, not exploit it."
        aire="3 / 1 / 4 / 3" pliante
      >
        <p>When AI entered the digital roadmap, most teams asked what it could <em>do</em>. I asked what it should <em>never</em> do - and put that on the table first.</p>
        <p>Before shipping AI-assisted features, I've asked the team to investigate, test prior to rolling anything at scale - to keep consistency, value and on-brand positioning across every product. AI wasn't just a new technology to embrace, but more a tool to add to our stack with responsible usage. And so got the community of practice sensitized too.</p>
        <p>An AI that nudges, manipulates, anchors on dark patterns or manufactures urgency isn't a feature, it's a breach of trust - and in healthcare, that trust isn't abstract. <strong>It starts with an employee and it finishes with a patient.</strong></p>
        <p>Not everyone shares this as a priority. I do. A system that shapes how people interact with their health has no business optimizing for engagement over honesty. Coherent and on-brand is the baseline. <strong>Ethical is the standard.</strong></p>
      </Conviction>

      <div class="compo__decor" aria-hidden="true" style="grid-area:3 / 3 / 4 / 4"><span class="compo__plat compo__plat--gris"></span></div>

      <Conviction
        id="pr-releases" rang="05" intitule="Releases" couleur="clair"
        titre="We break nothing without a bridge."
        aire="4 / 1 / 5 / 4" pliante
      >
        <p>With that many products depending on us, a careless breaking change is a tax paid 45 times over. So: <strong>one major release a year, maximum</strong> - protected, deliberate - and a steady cadence of improvements and fixes, roughly <strong>one release per two-week sprint</strong>.</p>
        <p>When a breaking change was unavoidable, we shipped a <strong>patch path</strong> alongside it and left product teams a real buffer to upgrade on their own schedule. The documentation was industrialized to match - at the component and the library level - structured to keep side effects from ever surprising a consumer.</p>
      </Conviction>

      <Conviction
        id="pr-support" rang="06" intitule="Support" couleur="rouge"
        titre="Support on their terms, not mine."
        aire="4 / 4 / 5 / 7" pliante
      >
        <p>The system serves the people building on it, so support flexed to them, not the other way around. <strong>Office hours</strong> for whoever wanted synchronous help; <strong>asynchronous support</strong> for whoever needed to move on their own clock - product teams kept full control over the urgency of their own problems.</p>
        <p>And communication was built to outgrow me. I kept it proactive and regular, but the point was always for the community to take the mic: <strong>members carrying the messages, answering each other directly</strong>, becoming the channel instead of routing everything through me.</p>
      </Conviction>

      {/* Le septieme occupe toute sa rangee : les six premiers disent comment
          le systeme tient, celui-ci comment l'equipe tient - et c'est la que
          la page va. */}
      <Conviction
        id="pr-owners" rang="07" intitule="Ownership" couleur="bleu"
        titre="A team of owners, not a team of hands."
        aire="5 / 1 / 6 / 7" pliante
      >
        <p>Inside the team, ownership was structural, not a pep talk. The <strong>support lead rotated every sprint</strong> - a model we didn't guess at but iterated into, reading the support and satisfaction data until the rotation was what the signal asked for - so responsibility, and recognition as the identified point of contact, moved around and no one got stuck in execution. Roles rotated. <strong>Sprint planning was collective</strong>, <strong>retros ran every sprint</strong>, and I sat in on the <strong>dailies</strong> as often as I could - mostly to absorb the hot updates coming down, so the team could stay in the work instead of the noise.</p>
        <p>All of it lived on <strong>Confluence</strong>, documented like a team mantra - so a new joiner became an owner fast, and the rest of Sanofi could see exactly how we worked. <strong>Transparency wasn't a value on a wall. It was the onboarding.</strong></p>
        <p>And growth didn't run top-down. It ran through the community: people levelled up by contributing, teaching, carrying the message - and I grew as much through them. <strong>Reverse mentoring by practice</strong> isn't a nice idea to me, it's how a system stays honest: the day you think you're the one who knows, you've stopped listening. <em>I lead, and I stay a student.</em></p>
      </Conviction>

      {/*
        LA CLOTURE, case blanche de la grille. Meme forme que sur Philosophy et
        que la citation de la landing : la phrase part du haut, le bouton
        descend en bas. Elle n'a pas de rang - c'est la sortie.
      */}
      <section class="conv conv--clair cloture" aria-labelledby="cloture-titre" style="grid-area:6 / 1 / 7 / 5">
        <span class="conv__plat" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="conv__txt cloture__dedans">
          <h2 id="cloture-titre">That's not the soft version of leadership. <em class="em-bleu">It's the operating system.</em></h2>
          <p class="cloture__corps">Seven principles, each with a practice behind it - and each one designed to keep working the day I stop running it. That's the whole test.</p>
          <Bouton variante="bleu" href="/philosophy">The convictions underneath →</Bouton>
        </div>
      </section>

      {/* Le carre jaune qui ferme la composition : la derniere rangee ne peut
          pas etre une bande de texte seule, ou elle cesse d'etre un Mondrian. */}
      <div class="compo__decor" aria-hidden="true" style="grid-area:6 / 5 / 7 / 7"><span class="compo__plat compo__plat--jaune"></span></div>

    </div>

  </div>

</Base>

<style is:global>
  /* ═══ Ce qui est propre a Operating System ═══ */

  /*
    LES BORDS GAUCHE ET DROIT SONT OUVERTS (BRIEF §3.2), comme sur Philosophy.
    .compo cerne la composition d'un filet de 1,5px qui ne se voit QUE contre
    une case blanche ; il barrait le flanc des cases claires et faisait lire la
    grille comme un tableau encadre. clip-path rogne un pixel de chaque cote,
    sans quoi le fond noir de la grille reapparait en un cheveu au sous-pixel.
    Le haut et le bas restent : ce sont eux qui detachent la composition du
    blanc de la page.
  */
  .compo--principes{border-left:0;border-right:0;clip-path:inset(0 1px 0 1px)}

  /*
    LA COMPOSITION DES SEPT PRINCIPES. Six colonnes, six rangees ; les colonnes
    3 et 6 sont fines et ne portent que du decor.

    Rangees en minmax : un titre qui gagne une ligne entre 861 et 1120 serait
    AVALE par la case, qui est en overflow:hidden, et une case qui s'ouvre doit
    pouvoir pousser sa rangee.

    Au-dessus du point de rupture seulement : etude.css remet la composition
    sur une colonne sous 860px, et cette declaration vit plus loin dans le
    bundle - a specificite egale elle gagnerait, media query comprise.
  */
  @media(min-width:861px){
    .compo--principes{grid-template-columns:24fr 18fr 6fr 22fr 24fr 6fr;
      grid-template-rows:minmax(190px,auto) minmax(140px,auto)
        minmax(170px,auto) minmax(190px,auto) minmax(170px,auto)
        minmax(260px,auto)}
  }

  /*
    ─── La cloture ───
    La phrase part du HAUT de la case et le bouton descend en bas avec
    margin-top:auto. Caler la phrase en bas renverrait tout le jeu de la rangee
    au-dessus d'elle, et le haut de la case vaudrait ce qui reste au lieu d'une
    valeur voulue - c'est la mesure faite sur la landing, et elle vaut ici.
  */
  .cloture{display:grid}
  .cloture__dedans{display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-start;
    gap:24px;padding:var(--pad-square)}
  .cloture__dedans .sb{margin-top:auto;align-self:flex-start}
  .cloture h2{margin:0;font-family:var(--display);font-size:var(--fs-section);
    font-weight:900;line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.015em}
  .cloture__corps{margin:0;font-size:var(--fs-body-s);line-height:1.7;
    color:var(--text-body);max-width:46ch}

  /*
    ─── Ce que le principe 03 emporte avec lui ───
    La citation et le surtitre de la sobriete etaient styles sous `.pan`. Les
    panneaux partis, ils vivent dans une case : les deux regles suivent, sans
    changer de valeurs. Le filet de la citation passe au noir - sur l'aplat
    jaune, le bleu de marque tombe a 4,67:1 contre 12,2 pour l'encre, et un
    filet decoratif se juge sur le meme pied qu'un indicateur.
  */
  .conv__detail .qt{margin:0;padding-left:20px;border-left:3px solid var(--text);
    font-size:var(--fs-body-s);line-height:1.65;font-style:italic}
  .conv__detail .eb{margin:0;font-size:var(--fs-eyebrow);font-weight:700;
    letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase}
</style>

<script>
  import { initConvictions } from '../scripts/convictions';
  initConvictions();
</script>
